              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "следствие (slédstviye) — \"a result, an outcome; an investigation\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Его болезнь — следствие стресса. Yegó bolézn — slédstviye stréssa. His illness is the result of stress."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Neuter, stressed on the first syllable. In law, следствие (slédstviye) is a criminal investigation."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "следствие (slédstviye) is built on след \"a track, a trail, a mark\" (EtymDB) with the suffix -ствие, a Church Slavonic pattern: a result follows its cause like a track."
            }
          ]
        },
