              "text": "в результате (v rezultáte) — \"as a result\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "В результате мы опоздали на поезд. V rezultáte my opozdáli na póyezd. As a result, we missed the train."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "With a noun it takes the genitive: в результате (v rezultáte) аварии. On its own it opens a sentence."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "в результате (v rezultáte) is в \"in\" with the prepositional of результат \"a result\", which is usually traced, through western languages, to Medieval Latin resultatum, built on resultāre \"to spring back\" (Lewis & Short)."
            }
          ]
        },
